@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Preserved desktop playback with library and OS fallback
hide footbox
autonumber
actor Contributor
participant "app : App" as App
participant "audio_utils\n<<module>>" as Audio
participant "File system" as Files
participant "soundfile / sounddevice" as Backend
participant "OS default player" as OS

note over App : Precondition: filename present and no unfinished recording.\nOtherwise the handler returns with appropriate feedback.
activate Contributor
Contributor -> App : play_pending_audio()\n(or _play_selected_audio())
activate App
App -> Audio : play_audio(resolved_path)
activate Audio
Audio -> Files : exists(path)
activate Files
Files --> Audio : exists: bool
deactivate Files
alt File does not exist
  note over Audio : Result = false; skip all playback attempts.
else File exists
  opt AUDIO_RECORDING_AVAILABLE
    Audio -> Backend : Stop prior library playback;\nsf.read(path); sd.play(data, sample_rate)
    activate Backend
    Backend --> Audio : Started or library exception
    deactivate Backend
  end
  alt Library playback started successfully
    note over Audio : Result = true; do not launch an OS player.
  else Library unavailable or failed
    Audio -> OS : Launch platform default player(path)
    activate OS
    OS --> Audio : Launch accepted or exception
    deactivate OS
    note over Audio : Result = true if launch accepted; otherwise false.
  end
end
Audio --> App : Result: bool
deactivate Audio
opt Result = false
  note over App : Show "Playback failed" error dialog.
end
App --> Contributor : Return; show an error only on failure
deactivate App
deactivate Contributor
legend bottom
  This is the desktop compatibility path, not the browser's private audio download flow.
  true means a playback request was accepted, not that sound was heard to completion.
  OS launch acceptance is not playback completion; media decoding is external.
  Expected audio errors are reported by the GUI; CSV is unchanged.
  Clear/close can stop in-process playback, not an external OS player's lifetime.
endlegend
@enduml
